   161	**(SD) Second-descent polynomiality.** If `delta'_{s'} = −1` and the child's top form has a MINOR
   162	point of multiplicity `u` (p.190: minor iff `u ≤ d'_{s'}/(n'−M'_{s'})`) whose minor-disc radius is
   163	`≥ v'/u`, `v' = d'_{s'} − u`, then Prop 6.3(1) — whose proof (p.197–198) is Jacobian-free — makes
   164	the grandchild `(P'', Q'')` POLYNOMIAL in `k[γ', π']`, and the p.198 chain rule with
   165	`J_{γ,π}(P,Q) = c γ^l` and `γ = (γ'^{−u} − e' − A'(γ') − π'γ'^{v'})/b'` gives
   166	
   167	```text
