   189	## 4. Why a second arithmetic generation cannot move the residual
   190	
   191	### 4.1 (B) is the parent's (12)/(13), verbatim
   192	
   193	With the roster's metric radii (own-data recipe, `pi <-> y`, `gamma <-> x`): for `i ≥ j` (first
   194	nonzero source index) `delta'_i = v − u/delta_i`, for `i < j` `delta'_i = v − u − (u/e)(1 − delta_i)`,
   195	`e = delta_j`. At `s = 3`, `u = 1`, `j = 2`: `L' = den(v − 1/delta_2) = num(delta_2)` and
   196	`L' delta'_1 = num(delta_2)(v−1) − den(delta_2)(1 − delta_1)`, so
   197	`A'_1 = den(den(delta_2)·delta_1) = A_1`; and `n'/d'_2 = n/d_2`, `m'/d'_2 = m/d_2`, `V'_2 = V_2`
   198	(D1 identity), so `N' = N`, `M' = M`. At `s ≥ 4` a zero-selected level `i` has `delta'_i = v − u/delta_i`
   199	integral whenever `u/delta_i ∈ Z`, so the child's `L'` omits that level's denominator — exactly the
   200	own-data lane's rule "a zero coefficient adds no denominator": `A'_1` is the parent's *actual*
   201	centre-stabilizer `A_1`, not Moh's (8) value. Numerically on the roster: **44 of 46 complete rows have `A'_1 = A_1` with Moh's (8) lattice and all 46 have `N' = N`, `M' = M`; the two exceptions R026, R028 (`s = 4`, zero-selected levels 3,4 whose child radii `−1, 0` are integral) have `A'_1 = 3, 2` against Moh-(8) `A_1 = 1`, which is exactly the own-data lane's *actual centre stabilizer* `A_1` (a zero coefficient adds no denominator) — the lattice `own_v_routes` already imposes at the parent's bottom; on the 20 prefixes 10 are equal and 10 have `A'_1 | A_1`**. For `u ≥ 2` the
   202	same computation gives `A'_1 | A_1`, so the child condition is *implied* by the parent's. (B) is
   203	therefore not a new condition anywhere in the census — it is the parent's bottom test transported,
   204	which is exactly what Lemma 6.2 (p.196, "*`x(θ) mod θ^q ∈ k((θ^{1/p})) ⟺ y(t) mod t^q ∈ k((t^{1/p}))`*")
   205	predicts: inversion preserves ramification.
   206	
   207	### 4.2 (GO) is inherited, (SD) is vacuous on ODE-screened rows
   208	
   209	*Inheritance.* The child's top pattern is the inversion image of the parent's level-`(s−1)`
   210	pattern (own-data `inverse_top`: the zero root goes to `W_0 = u·d_{s−1}/d_s − a·Σr`, each nonzero
   211	`b`-orbit of multiplicity `r` to `a` child roots of multiplicity `r`, `delta_{s−1} = a/b`), with the
   212	same threshold `lo' = d'_{s'}/(n'−M'_{s'}) = d_{s−1}/(n−M_{s−1})`. The orbit multiplicities `r ≠ lo`
   213	and "some `r > lo`" are literally the parent's ODE conditions; the child's new constraints are
   214	`W_0 ≠ lo` and `[W_0>0] + (a/gcd(a,u))·k ≤ Q'`, and every one of the 46 complete rows has an
   215	admissible image pattern (e.g. R019: parent `P=21,Q=15,A=7` with orbit `(3)` maps to child
   216	`z'=1`, orbit `(3)` at `A'=2`, distinct `3 ≤ 5`). Lower child levels have `P'_j = P_j`, `Q'_j = Q_j`
   217	exactly (`n'−M'_j` and `d'_{j+1}` both scale by `u/d_s`).
   218	
   219	*Vacuity of (SD).* At `u_s = 1`, `d'_{s'} = d_{s−1}/d_s` and `l = d_s − 3`, so at a simple minor
   220	point `l'' = d_{s−1}/d_s − d_s`. A kill needs `l'' < 0`, i.e. `d_{s−1} < d_s^2`, together with the
   221	SD hypothesis `delta'_{s'} = −1 ⟺ M_{s−1} = n − d_s(d_s−1)` and minority `1 ≤ lo_{s−1} =
   222	d_{s−1}/(n−M_{s−1}) = d_{s−1}/(d_s(d_s−1))`. Since `d_s | d_{s−1}`, the window is the single value
   223	`d_{s−1} = d_s(d_s−1)`, where `lo_{s−1} = 1` exactly — and then the parent's level-`(s−1)` ODE
   224	forbids any simple root (multiplicity `1 = P/Q` is excluded). So on every ODE-screened row (SD)
   225	at a simple point is empty, and (SD) at a heavy point (`u ≥ 2`) is conditional on the child's
   226	split window. On the 65 the boundary is populated: **20 rows have `l'' = 0`** (`d_{s−1} = d_s^2`:
   227	R002 R003 R004 R008 R013 R014 R017 R022 R030 R034 R036 R037 R039 R040 R041 R042 R046 R047 R048 R059),
   228	and the 8 rows with `l'' < 0` (R025–R028, R057, R058: `d_{s−1} = 12, d_s = 6`; R064; R066) all have
   229	the SD hypothesis failing (`delta'_{s'} ∈ {−2,−5}` or both top points major, `lo_top ∈ {2/5, 2/3}`).
