   290	**FALLACY-v2 ledger.** *Flag/place/series:* the child's `pi`-roots are the minor cluster's branches
   291	re-expanded at `y = ∞`; the child's top disc is NOT the parent's `D_{s−1}` (different clusters), and
   292	Sec. 4.2 uses only the inversion image, never an identification of discs. *Floor/attainment:* every
   293	pattern existence is a survival, never a witness pair; `l'' ≥ 0` is necessary, `l'' = 0` proves
   294	nothing (the Keller-grandchild reading was caught and withdrawn in Sec. 3). *Pole/interior:* (SD)
   295	is applied only after checking the vertex class (minor vs major point, p.190 threshold) and Prop
   296	6.3's `delta_s = −1`. *Variable/ring map:* the second-descent substitution is declared with its
   297	direction (`π = γ'^{−u}`, `γ = (π − e' − A' − π'γ'^{v'})/b'`) and its Jacobian is computed, not
   298	matched by name. *Prime label:* `'` and `''` are generation labels; no differentiation is meant
   299	except in `q'(a)`, which is Moh's own `d/dπ`. *Merge-free/M-descent:* prefixes keep their terminal
   300	index open; no `M'_{s'+1}` is invented. *Target/arrival index:* child level `j` is compared with
   301	parent level `j` for `P, Q` and with parent level `s−1` for the top pattern, and these are stated
   302	separately. No `sat()`, no Groebner run in this lane.
