+`eta=g(x,y)^(-1/n)`, with **x fixed**, and writes `f` as a series in `eta` with
+coefficients in `k[x]`. His definitions give
+
+```
+d_1=n,  d_i=gcd(n,M_1,...,M_{i-1}),
+M_i=min{a: f_a(x) != 0 and d_i does not divide a}.
+```
